"""Mutation check for the Step 16 dashboard. Break one line at a time; the tests must notice.
Run:  python tools/mutation_check_step16.py        (exit 0 = all killed in both files)

Targets:
  pipeline/dashboard_data.py    the decisions behind the screens    tests/test_dashboard_data.py
  pipeline/step16_dashboard.py  the screens                         tests/test_step16_dashboard.py
(the screen tests need `pip install streamlit`; they take about 15 seconds per mutation).

Not listed on purpose (no test could ever tell the difference):
  * the `, rowid` tie-break when reviews are read (two reviews written in the same second come
    back in write order anyway; the test that fixes the clock checks the visible result);
  * the `or ""` and `or default` guards for values that cannot be missing in a database made by
    the loader (a classified post always has text);
  * layout words only (column widths, `border=True`, page title, icons, button colours).
"""
